the single most common real-world defect class for exactly this UI pattern, and this codebase
has no framework-level guard against it (parseFormBool + a naive "OR the new value in" update
would have shipped it silently); confirmed clean by reading both the parse and the persist
layers end to end and by independently reading (not trusting the name of) the two-step
check-then-uncheck test.

VERDICT: PASS. No product defect found in SY2's own diff; one test-hardening observation
